<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_ScaldWreckScatter_Register.xml     UtinniPatches · authored 2026-09-13
  ============================================================================
  SCALD_MECHANICS_1 build pass, S6 — the registration half. RUT_ScaldWreckScatter.xml
  declares three GenStepDefs; a GenStepDef on its own runs on NO map, the
  same fact JawaResource_Scrapfields.xml and JawaGroundHulk_Register.xml (this
  same mod) already document and act on. This file is that listing, same
  three-file shape, same target.

  ===========================================================================
  SCOPE: Base_Player, GLOBAL — and that is deliberate, unlike the two prior
  registrations in this mod
  ===========================================================================
  JawaResource_Scrapfields.xml and JawaGroundHulk_Register.xml both scope to
  Base_Player for CONTINUITY reasons (one wreck, one clan's own ship; scrap
  belongs on the settled map only). This registration has a different, and
  simpler, justification: the wreck scatter's OWN terrain validator
  (terrainValidationAllowed -> RUT_ScaldShallow) already confines it to
  cells carrying that tag, and only the Scald's own three shallow water
  terrains carry it (RUT_ScaldWater.xml, this same pass) — nowhere else in
  the load order does. Registering onto Base_Player (rather than the
  abstract MapCommonBase) is still the right call for the same reason the
  other two registrations give: the player's own settled map is where a
  wrecks-in-the-shallows scatter should visibly land, not every encounter
  or quest map layered over the abstract base.

  ===========================================================================
  THE TARGET, READ FROM CORE
  ===========================================================================
  Core/Defs/MapGeneration/BasePlayerMapGenerator.xml:4-15,
  MapGeneratorDef ParentName="MapCommonBase" Name="Base_Player", <genSteps>
  a plain list of GenStepDef names — <li> is correct, read from the node
  directly (same citation JawaResource_Scrapfields.xml already gives).

  ===========================================================================
  SAFETY
  ===========================================================================
  No MayRequire needed on this patch or its target GenStepDefs — unlike
  JawaGroundHulk_Register.xml, nothing here depends on another mod being
  present; RUT_ScaldWreckScatter.xml's three GenStepDefs are this mod's own,
  always loaded together with this patch. Conditional test xpath is
  IDENTICAL to the inner Add's xpath (JawaResource_Scrapfields.xml's own
  discipline): if Core ever renames Base_Player or restructures the node,
  this becomes a silent no-op rather than a red error.

  Held via src/DEPLOY_HOLD.txt together with RUT_ScaldWrecks.xml and
  RUT_ScaldWreckScatter.xml: deploying this patch without the ThingDefs it
  names would add three defNames to Base_Player's genSteps that resolve to
  nothing in the running game — a dangling cross-reference on every map
  generation, not a smaller failure than the missing art itself.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/MapGeneratorDef[defName="Base_Player"]/genSteps</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/MapGeneratorDef[defName="Base_Player"]/genSteps</xpath>
      <value>
        <li>RUT_Jawa_ScatterScaldWreckHull</li>
        <li>RUT_Jawa_ScatterScaldWreckTank</li>
        <li>RUT_Jawa_ScatterScaldWreckFrame</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
